<title>GERMANY: German air cargo up 8.5pct Apr, up 6.5pct Jan-Apr.</title>
<headline>German air cargo up 8.5pct Apr, up 6.5pct Jan-Apr.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German air cargo market grew 8.5 percent in April to 172,320 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>German air cargo exports grew 10.6 percent in April while imports increased 6.7 percent, the monthly ADV traffic report said.</p>
<p>The fastest-growing airports last month were Duesseldorf, Munich, Berlin and Cologne, it showed.</p>
<p>The German air cargo market grew 6.5 percent to 673,251 tonnes over the first four months of the year, the report added.</p>
<p>Details in tonnes and percent changes from 1996 include:</p>
<p>				   Apr'97	 Pct change</p>
<p>  Total flown cargo	 173,320	   Up  8.5</p>
<p>  Exports			87,825	   Up 10.6</p>
<p>  Imports			80,538	   Up  6.7</p>
<p>  Transit			 3,957		n/a</p>
<p>				Jan-Apr '97     Pct change</p>
<p>  Total flown cargo	 673,251	   Up 6.5</p>
<p>  Exports		     335,465	   Up 6.8</p>
<p>  Imports		     317,112	   Up 5.4</p>
<p>  Transit			20,674		n/a</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
